```java
public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    // Check if n is positive and within the range of an integer
    if (n <= 0 || n > Integer.MAX_VALUE) {
        return false;
    }
    // Check if n is a power of three by checking if it is divisible by 3 repeatedly
    while (n % 3 == 0) {
        n /= 3;
    }
    return n == 1;
}
```

This solution works by checking if `n` is positive and within the range of an integer, and then repeatedly dividing `n` by 3 until it is no longer divisible by 3. If the result of the division is 1, then `n` is a power of three. Otherwise, it is not a power of three. This approach is based on the fact that a power of three can only be divided by 3 repeatedly until it becomes 1, and any other integer will not reach 1 in this process.

